---
/**
 * The seam between two home-page sections (2026-10-11).
 *
 * It replaces a full-bleed `border-block-start` on each section, which ran
 * edge to edge through the gutters and the bookmarks and read as a leftover
 * table rule rather than as part of the design. Since 2026-11-03 it is short
 * and centred: a hairline of a few rem on either side of the brand's
 * three-part bar — the same mark the headings use, at its small size.
 *
 * It is rendered BETWEEN sections, so it sits exactly at the boundary, i.e.
 * at the midpoint of the gap both sections share. It takes no height of its
 * own, so the rhythm in `HomePage.astro` is unchanged. Two seams in a row
 * (a section that rendered nothing, like `CustomerCases` without a case)
 * collapse to one.
 */
---

<div class="lp-seam lp-container" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="lp-seam__line"></span>
  <span class="tds-brandbar tds-brandbar--sm lp-seam__mark"></span>
  <span class="lp-seam__line lp-seam__line--end"></span>
</div>

<style>
  /* Short and centred since 2026-11-03 (asked for): two hairlines a few
     rem long either side of the brand mark, instead of rules across the
     whole content width. Solid, rounded ends; no fade (no gradients). */
  .lp-seam {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    height: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .lp-seam + .lp-seam {
    display: none;
  }
  .lp-seam__line {
    flex: none;
    width: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    height: 1px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--color-line);
  }
  .lp-seam__mark {
    flex: none;
  }
</style>
